# Docker environment setup for Hell Let Loose Map Switcher

## Docker Environment Variables

Required environment variables for Docker deployment:

### Single Server Setup

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name hll-map-switcher \
  -v $(pwd)/data:/app/data \
  -e DISCORD_TOKEN=your_discord_bot_token \
  -e DISCORD_GUILD_ID=your_discord_guild_id \
  -e DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=your_discord_channel_id \
  -e API_ENDPOINT=your_api_endpoint \
  -e MAPS_API_KEY=your_maps_api_key \
  -e SERVER_NAME=Your Server Name \
  -e CRCON_BASE_URL=https://your-crcon-host/api \
  -e CRCON_TOKEN=crcon-django-token \
  hll-map-switcher
```

### Multiple Servers Setup

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name hll-map-switcher \
  -v $(pwd)/data:/app/data \
  -e DISCORD_TOKEN=your_discord_bot_token \
  -e DISCORD_GUILD_ID=your_discord_guild_id \
  -e DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=your_discord_channel_id \
  -e API_ENDPOINT=your_api_endpoint \
  -e MAPS_API_KEY=your_maps_api_key \
  -e SERVER1_NAME=Server 1 \
  -e SERVER1_CRCON_BASE_URL=https://crcon1.example.com/api \
  -e SERVER1_CRCON_TOKEN=token1 \
  -e SERVER2_NAME=Server 2 \
  -e SERVER2_CRCON_BASE_URL=https://crcon2.example.com/api \
  -e SERVER2_CRCON_TOKEN=token2 \
  hll-map-switcher
```

## Environment Variable Reference

### Discord Configuration

- `DISCORD_TOKEN`: Bot authentication token from Discord Developer Portal
- `DISCORD_GUILD_ID`: Target guild ID for command registration (optional)
- `DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID`: Channel ID where control panel will be posted (optional for auto-discovery)

### API Configuration

- `API_ENDPOINT`: Your HLL API endpoint URL
- `MAPS_API_KEY`: Maps API key for map catalog access

### Server Configuration

#### Single Server

- `SERVER_NAME`: Human-readable server name (defaults to "HLL Server")
- `CRCON_BASE_URL`: CRCON HTTP API base URL (e.g., `https://crcon.example.com/api`)
- `CRCON_TOKEN`: CRCON authentication token
- `RCON_HOST`: Optional RCON server hostname
- `RCON_PORT`: Optional RCON server port (default: 12345)
- `RCON_PASSWORD`: Optional RCON server password

#### Multiple Servers

Use numbered prefixes for multiple servers:

- `SERVER{N}_NAME`: Server name (e.g., `SERVER1_NAME=Production Server`)
- `SERVER{N}_CRCON_BASE_URL`: CRCON base URL for server N
- `SERVER{N}_CRCON_TOKEN`: CRCON token for server N
- `SERVER{N}_RCON_HOST`: Optional RCON host for server N
- `SERVER{N}_RCON_PORT`: Optional RCON port for server N
- `SERVER{N}_RCON_PASSWORD`: Optional RCON password for server N

### Optional Settings

- `WARFARE_MATCH_TIMER_MINUTES`: Default warfare match timer (default: 90)
- `WARFARE_WARMUP_TIMER_MINUTES`: Default warfare warmup timer (default: 3)
- `DEBUG`: Enable debug logging (true/false)

## Docker Compose Environment

For Docker Compose deployment, use `.env` file with the same variables:

```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  hll-map-switcher:
    build: .
    container_name: hll-map-switcher
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      - DISCORD_TOKEN=${DISCORD_TOKEN}
      - DISCORD_GUILD_ID=${DISCORD_GUILD_ID}
      - DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=${DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID}
      - API_ENDPOINT=${API_ENDPOINT}
      - MAPS_API_KEY=${MAPS_API_KEY}
      - SERVER_NAME=${SERVER_NAME}
      - CRCON_BASE_URL=${CRCON_BASE_URL}
      - CRCON_TOKEN=${CRCON_TOKEN}
    volumes:
      - ./data:/app/data
    env_file:
      - .env
```

## Configuration Files

### requirements.txt

```text
discord.py==2.6.4
python-dotenv==1.0.1
requests==2.32.3
```

### .env.example.single

Copy to `.env` for local development:

```env
# Discord Settings
DISCORD_TOKEN=your_discord_bot_token
DISCORD_GUILD_ID=your_discord_guild_id
DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=your_discord_channel_id

# Single Server Configuration
SERVER_NAME=Your Server Name

# CRCON HTTP API
CRCON_BASE_URL=https://your-crcon-host/api
CRCON_TOKEN=crcon-django-token

# Optional direct game-server RCON fallback
RCON_HOST=your-game-server-host
RCON_PORT=12345
RCON_PASSWORD=your_rcon_password

# Optional Settings
WARFARE_MATCH_TIMER_MINUTES=90
WARFARE_WARMUP_TIMER_MINUTES=3
DEBUG=True
```

### .env.example.multiple

Copy to `.env` for multi-server setup:

```env
# Discord Settings
DISCORD_TOKEN=your_discord_bot_token
